" in that period. Investors are demanding more yield, but they are still buying.\n- **Equity is closed to the largest issuer.** Equity markets have been less receptive. Two utility share offerings were cut back in Q3. Pellham Power pulled its C$2.4B offering on 14 October. Pellham is the largest buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n- **Pellham is cutting its own plan.** Pellham said it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and resize its Q1 2027 tender. That suggests debt alone isn't enough to fund the full plan as filed.\n- **Evidence gaps.** I did not find the actual 2027 capex amounts, which are in the utility tender calendar. I also did not find Pellham's debt capacity, such as its leverage or rating headroom. So I can't say how large the funding gap is. I only have one data point on debt, the Norvane deal, and none for Pellham.\n\nThe conclusion is that Norvane-type issuers can likely fund through bonds at higher cost. Pellham probably can't fund the full plan that way. A pulled equity raise followed by a 40% order cut points to a binding funding constraint.\n\nThe equity question was handled separately in n8.r1.","ttft_ms":2208,"type":"result","duration_ms":37971,"uuid":"a88e5a5a-b126-4275-8ced-d547b843e63b","ttft_stream_ms":1108,"time_to_request_ms":232,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":23,"system_prompt":12,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":31,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":5,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":26,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":18,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":44,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":15,"tool_schema_build":10,"message_normalization":7,"client_creation":6,"request_build":16},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":117,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":69,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":187,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":113,"process_rs